From: f <f@f>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8450: drop three reserved regions the
 vendor's tree does not have

Three regions of the SoC's reserved memory are not in the device tree
the phone ships with: mte_mem (512 MiB at 0xc0000000),
trusted_apps_mem (57 MiB) and trusted_apps_ext_mem (59 MiB). Linux never
used that memory: 628 MiB of the 12 GB, the larger part of the
difference between the 10.1 GiB the phone reports and what Android
had.

Upstream removed the three nodes from sm8450.dtsi after 7.2.10 ("not
present on downstream device trees and only take memory away from the
AP"); the diff is theirs, on the file as this tree has it. The vendor's
trees were read for this phone before writing this: the 13 base trees
of the stock vendor_boot.img and the 45 overlays of dtbo.img
(diting_images_OS3.0.3.0.VLFCNXM_15.0) have no reserved region at any
of the three addresses, and the overlay of diting adds none at all.

Experimental until it has run on the phone: nothing here says the
hypervisor leaves these regions alone, only that Android used them as
ordinary memory on this very device.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi | 15 ---------------
 1 file changed, 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8450.dtsi
@@ -760,11 +760,6 @@
 			no-map;
 		};
 
-		mte_mem: memory@c0000000 {
-			reg = <0x0 0xc0000000 0x0 0x20000000>;
-			no-map;
-		};
-
 		qheebsp_reserved_mem: memory@e0000000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0xe0000000 0x0 0x600000>;
 			no-map;
@@ -812,18 +807,9 @@
 
 		qtee_mem: memory@e9b00000 {
 			reg = <0x0 0xe9b00000 0x0 0x500000>;
-			no-map;
-		};
-
-		trusted_apps_mem: memory@ea000000 {
-			reg = <0x0 0xea000000 0x0 0x3900000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
 
-		trusted_apps_ext_mem: memory@ed900000 {
-			reg = <0x0 0xed900000 0x0 0x3b00000>;
-			no-map;
-		};
 	};
 
 	smp2p-adsp {
